---
import Service from '../layouts/Service.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Can my deck hold a hot tub?', a: 'A deck has to be designed for a hot tub. A filled tub with people in it is very heavy, so we plan extra footings, closer joist spacing or a steel frame under that spot. We design the deck around the tub from the start rather than adding it later.' },
  { q: 'Should the hot tub be recessed into the deck?', a: 'A recessed tub sits with its rim at deck level, so you step down into the water and it looks built-in. A surround keeps the tub on a pad or the deck with composite steps around it, which is easier to service. We help you choose based on your yard and tub.' },
  { q: 'Can you build for a sauna or cold plunge?', a: 'Yes. We have built decks for barrel saunas and cold plunges as well as hot tubs, including a Sundance cabin deck with a sauna, hot tub and waterfall bench.' },
  { q: 'How do you add privacy around a hot tub?', a: 'TimberTech HideAway privacy screens, privacy railing panels and privacy walls block the neighbors’ view while keeping the deck open to the sky.' },
];
---
<Service
  slug="hot-tub-decks"
  name="Hot Tub Decks"
  title="Hot Tub Deck Builder in Utah | Spa, Sauna Decks | TC Decks"
  description="Hot tub, sauna and cold plunge decks in Utah County and Salt Lake County, framed for the weight with composite decking, privacy screens and step lights."
  h1="Hot tub, sauna and cold plunge decks"
  lead="A hot tub deck has to carry a lot of weight, stay safe with wet feet, and be pleasant on a snowy January night. We design the deck around your tub, sauna or plunge from the very start."
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <h2>Framed for the weight</h2>
  <p>A filled hot tub is one of the heaviest things you can put on a deck. We plan the framing and footings under it for that load, with extra footings, closer joist spacing, or a <a href="/steel-deck-framing">steel frame</a> built for the job. If the tub sits on a slab, we build the deck around it instead.</p>

  <Photo src="/images/projects/highland-english-walnut-hideaway/timber-pavilion-metal-roof-hot-tub-deck" alt="Hot tub deck under a timber pavilion with a metal roof in Highland, Utah" />

  <h2>Recessed or surround</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Recessed:</strong> the deck is built up to the rim of the tub, so it looks built-in and you step down into the water.</li>
    <li><strong>Surround:</strong> the tub sits on a pad or the deck, with composite steps and a skirt wrapped around it. Easier to service and great for patios.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Either way we leave access panels so the tub's equipment can be serviced.</p>

  <h2>Hot tub decks we've built</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/project-showcase#highland-english-walnut-hideaway">Highland:</a> a backyard retreat built around two hot tubs, with TimberTech Vintage English Walnut, a timber-frame pavilion, HideAway privacy screens and lights on every step.</li>
    <li><a href="/project-showcase#sundance-cabin-english-walnut">Sundance:</a> a mountain cabin deck for a barrel sauna and a hot tub, with a curved waterfall bench and black privacy screens.</li>
    <li><a href="/project-showcase#south-jordan-fiber-optic-privacy">South Jordan:</a> a covered second-story deck with fiber optic lights in the underside, so the hot tub patio below glows like a starry sky.</li>
    <li><a href="/project-showcase#pleasant-grove-trex-slide">Pleasant Grove:</a> a magazine-cover Trex deck with the hot tub on the covered patio underneath.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="grid grid-2">
    <Photo sizes="grid-3" src="/images/projects/sundance-cabin-english-walnut/sauna-and-hot-tub-deck-waterfall-bench-mountains" alt="Sauna and hot tub deck with a waterfall bench in Sundance, Utah" />
    <Photo sizes="grid-3" src="/images/ideas/hot-tub-deck-steps" alt="Hot tub framed into a composite deck with wrap-around steps" />
  </div>

  <h2>Privacy, lighting and winter use</h2>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> HideAway screens, privacy railing panels and walls block sight lines without closing in the deck.</li>
    <li><strong>Lighting:</strong> step, riser and recessed lights keep wet-foot trips safe at night. See our <a href="/design-ideas/lighting">lighting ideas</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Materials:</strong> TimberTech and Trex boards don't rot, resist stains and stay slip-resistant when wet.</li>
    <li><strong>Winter:</strong> a short, lit path from the back door and a place to sit between soaks make the tub easy to use all winter. A <a href="/covered-decks">covered deck</a> keeps snow off.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Read more in <a href="/blog/hot-tub-cold-plunge-and-sauna-decks">Hot tub, cold plunge and sauna decks in Utah</a>, then <a href="/contact">call for a free estimate</a> and tell us what you'd like to include.</p>
</Service>
